Filey changes to PdfCraft's web app (Office work > PDF): the control bridge
(apps/pdfcraft-web: pdfcraftControl) that lets the Filey agent drive it with PdfCraft's UI control
channel, printing handed to Filey (fileyPrintPdf), and the app named "PDF" where users see it
(credit to PdfCraft kept in About and on Home, no community button or card in the web build),
wheel zoom scaled for browser wheel deltas (a notch was a 2.7x jump), and side panes that
start closed so the page has room in a Filey tab. The session gets the page's clock and time zone
(Session::with_wall_clock): the web build has none, so stamps read "Jan 00, 0" and comments
and saves carried no date.
Files go in and out through PdfCraft's own ?host=parent bridge.
Upstream: https://github.com/storytold/pdfcraft commit f0c9901c398372782a4eb001c95638289a5edab0 (main). MIT OR Apache-2.0.

Build: git apply filey-control.patch; cd apps/pdfcraft-web; trunk build --release
Install: node scripts/fetch-office-apps.mjs --app pdfcraft --from <pdfcraft>/dist/web (copy LICENSE-MIT/APACHE in first)

